Package: radioberry
Architecture: arm64
Depends:
 ${shlibs:Depends},
 ${misc:Depends},
 radioberry-dkms (= ${source:Version}),
 systemd,
 udev,
Description: RadioBerry 2.x HF transceiver on the Raspberry Pi 5
 radioberryd serves a RadioBerry 2.x HAT to SDR clients over openHPSDR
 Protocol 1 (Hermes-Lite 2 dialect) and Protocol 2, as
 radioberry.service. Transmit and the PA are off as installed; see
 /etc/radioberry/config.yaml.
 .
 Also included: the RadioBerry gateware (Hermes-Lite 2 PIO variants,
 built from source), the device tree overlay, and the tools rbprobe,
 rbcat, rbctl, rbload, p1probe and p2probe. The kernel driver is in
 radioberry-dkms.

Package: radioberry-dkms
Architecture: all
Depends:
 ${misc:Depends},
 dkms,
Recommends:
 linux-headers-rpi-2712 | linux-headers-rpi-v8,
Description: RadioBerry 2.x kernel driver (DKMS source)
 The radioberry.ko driver for the RadioBerry 2.x on the Raspberry Pi 5:
 loads the gateware, streams receive and transmit through the RP1 PIO,
 and gives userspace /dev/radioberry. DKMS builds it for each installed
 kernel and rebuilds it when the kernel is updated.

Package: radioberry-dev
Architecture: all
Depends:
 ${misc:Depends},
Description: RadioBerry 2.x driver ABI header
 radioberry_ioctl.h: the /dev/radioberry interface of the radioberry.ko
 driver, for programs that use the device directly.
